[{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4228965656","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/118283#issuecomment-4228965656","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/118283","id":4228965656,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc78EOUY","user":{"login":"syntaxerror247","id":176927541,"node_id":"U_kgDOCouzNQ","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/176927541?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/syntaxerror247","html_url":"https://github.com/syntaxerror247","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/syntaxerror247/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/syntaxerror247/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/syntaxerror247/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/syntaxerror247/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/syntaxerror247/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/syntaxerror247/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/syntaxerror247/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/syntaxerror247/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/syntaxerror247/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-04-11T08:08:07Z","updated_at":"2026-04-11T08:08:07Z","body":"@Alex2782 Have you ever tested godot's obb support?","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4228965656/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4237199592","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/118283#issuecomment-4237199592","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/118283","id":4237199592,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc78jojo","user":{"login":"Alex2782","id":41921395,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQxOTIxMzk1","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/41921395?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Alex2782","html_url":"https://github.com/Alex2782","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Alex2782/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Alex2782/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Alex2782/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Alex2782/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Alex2782/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Alex2782/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Alex2782/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Alex2782/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Alex2782/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-04-13T14:34:57Z","updated_at":"2026-04-13T14:34:57Z","body":"> @Alex2782 Have you ever tested godot's obb support?\r\n\r\nNo, a week ago I didn't even know what `obb` was 😃 ","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4237199592/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":1,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4238050205","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/118283#issuecomment-4238050205","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/118283","id":4238050205,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc78m4Od","user":{"login":"dsnopek","id":191561,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5MTU2MQ==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/191561?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/dsnopek","html_url":"https://github.com/dsnopek","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dsnopek/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dsnopek/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dsnopek/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dsnopek/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dsnopek/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dsnopek/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dsnopek/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dsnopek/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dsnopek/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-04-13T16:34:59Z","updated_at":"2026-04-13T16:34:59Z","body":"> As I mentioned in the last meeting, I strongly believe that we should consider removing OBB support altogether. The Play Store deprecated it in 2021, and Godot 4 was released in 2023.\r\n\r\nWhile other app stores are not nearly as important as the Google Play store, it's probably worth checking if OBB support is needed for any of the more important/interesting ones\r\n\r\nFor a few that I've personally used:\r\n\r\n- The Meta (Horizon) store supports OBBs, but they also provide a custom system that is easier to use ([\"required asset files\"](https://developers.meta.com/horizon/documentation/unity/ps-assets/#required-asset-files))\r\n- The Amazon Appstore (for Kindle Fire devices) [doesn't support OBBs](https://developer.amazon.com/docs/app-submission/understanding-submission.html#apk_file_size_limitations)\r\n- The Samsung Galaxy store: I couldn't find definitive documentation about OBBs, but per [the FAQ](https://developer.samsung.com/galaxy-store/faq.html), they support AABs, so I would suspect that OBB support isn't needed (even if it's supported)\r\n\r\nSo, for just those ones, we don't need OBB support :-)\r\n\r\nI'm not sure if there's any others worth researching?","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4238050205/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4238231569","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/118283#issuecomment-4238231569","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/118283","id":4238231569,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc78nkgR","user":{"login":"m4gr3d","id":914968,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjkxNDk2OA==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/914968?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/m4gr3d","html_url":"https://github.com/m4gr3d","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/m4gr3d/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/m4gr3d/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/m4gr3d/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/m4gr3d/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/m4gr3d/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/m4gr3d/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/m4gr3d/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/m4gr3d/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/m4gr3d/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-04-13T17:06:58Z","updated_at":"2026-04-13T17:06:58Z","body":"> > As I mentioned in the last meeting, I strongly believe that we should consider removing OBB support altogether. The Play Store deprecated it in 2021, and Godot 4 was released in 2023.\r\n> \r\n> While other app stores are not nearly as important as the Google Play store, it's probably worth checking if OBB support is needed for any of the more important/interesting ones\r\n> \r\n> For a few that I've personally used:\r\n> \r\n> * The Meta (Horizon) store supports OBBs, but they also provide a custom system that is easier to use ([\"required asset files\"](https://developers.meta.com/horizon/documentation/unity/ps-assets/#required-asset-files))\r\n> * The Amazon Appstore (for Kindle Fire devices) [doesn't support OBBs](https://developer.amazon.com/docs/app-submission/understanding-submission.html#apk_file_size_limitations)\r\n> * The Samsung Galaxy store: I couldn't find definitive documentation about OBBs, but per [the FAQ](https://developer.samsung.com/galaxy-store/faq.html), they support AABs, so I would suspect that OBB support isn't needed (even if it's supported)\r\n> \r\n> So, for just those ones, we don't need OBB support :-)\r\n> \r\n> I'm not sure if there's any others worth researching?\r\n\r\n@dsnopek The issue (and reason for deprecating) is that our current implementation is specific to the play store.\r\nIt makes use of Google's [`com.android.vending.licensing` and `com.google.android.vending` libraries](https://developer.android.com/google/play/expansion-files#AboutLibraries) and requires a [public key that can only be provided by the Play store](https://developer.android.com/google/play/licensing/setting-up).","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4238231569/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4241664785","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/118283#issuecomment-4241664785","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/118283","id":4241664785,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc780qsR","user":{"login":"syntaxerror247","id":176927541,"node_id":"U_kgDOCouzNQ","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/176927541?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/syntaxerror247","html_url":"https://github.com/syntaxerror247","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/syntaxerror247/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/syntaxerror247/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/syntaxerror247/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/syntaxerror247/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/syntaxerror247/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/syntaxerror247/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/syntaxerror247/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/syntaxerror247/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/syntaxerror247/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-04-14T06:18:15Z","updated_at":"2026-04-14T06:21:44Z","body":"> > As I mentioned in the last meeting, I strongly believe that we should consider removing OBB support altogether. The Play Store deprecated it in 2021, and Godot 4 was released in 2023.\r\n> \r\n> While other app stores are not nearly as important as the Google Play store, it's probably worth checking if OBB support is needed for any of the more important/interesting ones\r\n\r\nThe current implementation is already broken, it doesn't work with manually placed obb files.\r\nI tried using it with Godot 4.6, the manually placed obb file gets deleted on app start and game tries to download it but can't because it's not on play store.\r\n\r\nAnd we never got any bug reports for this, which probably means that no one's using it :-)","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4241664785/reactions","total_count":2,"+1":2,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4251350340","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/118283#issuecomment-4251350340","issue_